task: timeout-masks-failure
agent: fable-fusion
started: 2026-09-09
branch: feature/timeout-masks-failure
worktree: ../okay-wt-timeout
spec: specs/cross-platform-async.md (timeout's law, to be added) — BACKLOG entry

why: Async.timeout(ms)(p) = race(p.map(Some), sleep(ms).map(None)), and
  race lets a FAILING contender lose without ending the race, so a
  program that fails at once under timeout answers None after the
  whole ms with its exception replaced. Found by resilience-http (a
  breaker's refusal under Deadline.enforce became a 504 after 5 s).
what: the law "a failure ends a timeout at once, with its own
  exception" — the test on Async.timeout FIRST (it must FAIL on the
  current tree, per no-failing-test-no-fix), then timeout changed,
  race untouched (its contract is stated and tested). Cross-platform:
  the same test on JVM, JS, Native (cross suite).
